  "coverageRules": [
    "Every one of the eight window concepts is visually checked with its default thread concept in every core configuration, with the fake application rail open and closed.",
    "Every one of the eight thread concepts is visually checked in at least one host window in every core configuration; two structurally different host windows are preferred.",
    "All sixty-four within-agent window and thread pairings receive an automated mount and console-error smoke test. Full visual review of all pairings is not required.",
    "Docked and pop-out mounts are exercised. State must survive changing mounts.",
    "Every core feature state is captured and visually reviewed across all thirty-two theme-width configurations for the selected required host pairing.",
    "Reduced-motion behavior is tested separately for every motion-bearing interaction.",
    "Automated geometry checks do not replace visual inspection."
  ],
  "automatedAssertions": [
    "no horizontal overflow",
    "no clipped prose",
